course: dictionary
lesson: 10361
title: Trash: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning depending on where you are and who is speaking. «Trash» is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning is being used. In «Please take out the trash», the clue is the bag and the bin, so trash means rubbish, the things you throw away.
explain: «That film is trash» has no bin in it. The clue is the word film, so trash here means something of very poor quality. «He trashed the room» tells you that trash can also be a verb: to trash something means to damage it badly or make a big mess of it.
explain: Trash can also be an insult. Calling a person «trash» is rude and hurtful. Boxers sometimes use «trash talk» before a match to sell tickets, but that is a show, and it does not make insults okay at school.
fact: In American and Canadian English, trash means rubbish, the things you throw away.
fact: «Trash» can also mean something of very poor quality, as in «that film is trash».
fact: To trash something means to damage it badly or make a big mess of it, as in «trashed the room».
fact: To trash someone means to criticise them harshly, and calling a person «trash» is an insult.
fact: Most computers move deleted files to the Recycle Bin or Trash first, and they can be got back until it is emptied.
exercise: «Please take out the trash.» Where would people most likely say this? | *The US or Canada | Australia | The UK | Ireland
exercise: «He trashed the room before dinner.» What does trashed mean here? | Locked the door | Painted it bright blue | *Made a terrible mess of it | Cleaned it very carefully
exercise: Lisa says «That film is trash.» What does she mean? | It is a film about boxing | It is full of rubbish from the dump | It is the funniest film ever made | *It is of very poor quality
test: In «That film is trash», what does trash mean? | To damage something badly | Very old | Rubbish that is thrown away | *Something of very poor quality
test: Why is calling someone «trash» an insult? | Because trash is the same as gold | Because it means they are a boxer | *Because it is rude and hurts their feelings | Because it means they are very rich
exam: Jayden reads «Most computers move deleted files to the Recycle Bin or Trash first.» What does Trash mean here? | Very poor quality work | A big mess in a room | *A place where deleted files wait before they are emptied | A harsh criticism of someone
